# Write a program to calculate area of a triangle using Heron's formula.
# Heron's formula: area = sqrt(S*(S-a)*(S-b)*(S-c))
a = float(input("Enter the first side of triangle: "))
b = float(input("Enter the second side of triangle: "))
c = float(input("Enter the third side of triangle: "))
S = (a+b+c)/2
area = (S*(S-a)*(S-b)*(S-c))**0.5
print("Area of the triangle: " + str(area))
#output:
#  Area of the triangle: 56.568542494923804



